WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.333
Okay, Cyllage City, you’re up next!

2
00:00:07.399 --> 00:00:09.066
- Here we come!
- Pikachu!

3
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.866
- I have an idea!
- Huh?

4
00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:13.399
Since we’re already here in Lumiose City,

5
00:00:13.466 --> 00:00:16.900
why don’t we go and visit Professor Sycamore before we leave?

6
00:00:16.966 --> 00:00:20.500
- That’s a great idea, Serena!
- Uh-huh!

7
00:00:20.566 --> 00:00:22.666
Also... Ta-da!

8
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:26.933
- I baked macarons last night!
- Yummy and pretty, too!

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.833
- Let’s share them with the professor.
- Yay! Oh, boy, I can hardly wait!

10
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:43.033
- Huh? What’s that?
- Amazing. Fascinating!

11
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.666
It would seem this is Blaziken’s Mega Evolution.

12
00:00:46.733 --> 00:00:50.766
Mega Evolution? It looks mega-super-strong!

13
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:52.833
To refresh our collective memory,

14
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.866
our plan is to make Meowth Mega Evolve and then capture Pikachu.

15
00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:00.500
- Wobbuffet!
- Yeah, but is that even possible?

16
00:01:00.566 --> 00:01:03.033
I’ve also discovered that Professor Sycamore

17
00:01:03.099 --> 00:01:05.633
is the leading expert on Mega Evolution.

18
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.233
So, all we do is we steal his data.

19
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.433
And program said data into our detailed database!

20
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.533
Dig! Now I understand why we brought that monstrosity with us!

21
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.600
Mega Evolution makes the Mega Meowth.

22
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:19.399
Mega Meowth makes the Mega Team Rocket.

23
00:01:19.466 --> 00:01:22.066
Mega Team Rocket makes the whole Mega world its own!

24
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.933
- Run that by me that again?
- No need! It’s Mega-mania!

25
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.700
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

26
00:01:28.766 --> 00:01:32.466
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

27
00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:35.133
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

28
00:01:35.199 --> 00:01:38.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

29
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.300
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

30
00:01:41.366 --> 00:01:44.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

31
00:01:44.566 --> 00:01:47.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

32
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.733
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

33
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

34
00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:55.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

35
00:02:05.533 --> 00:02:07.366
While traveling in the Kalos region,

36
00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:09.500
as Ash works to enter the Kalos League,

37
00:02:09.566 --> 00:02:13.000
our heroes have decided to visit Professor Sycamore.

38
00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:17.500
So you’re all traveling together now, eh? Sounds like a great plan!

39
00:02:17.566 --> 00:02:19.366
- Thanks!
- Pika!

40
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:23.833
Professor! Here! I baked delicious macarons for everyone!

41
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.633
Mm! Such a sweet treat!

42
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.500
How nice! I suggest we have a little tea break with those macarons.

43
00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:34.200
I still have work to do, so I’ll have mine a bit later.

44
00:02:34.266 --> 00:02:36.533
Will you let us see what you’re working on?

45
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.633
Of course! Make yourself at home.

46
00:02:40.933 --> 00:02:43.233
Everyone, tea is ready!

47
00:02:43.299 --> 00:02:45.400
All right, everybody, let’s dig in!

48
00:02:45.466 --> 00:02:48.600
- Hey, where are the macaroons?
- Huh?

49
00:02:48.666 --> 00:02:50.400
- Pika! Pika?
- Where did they go?

50
00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:52.500
- They were here a moment ago.
- Huh?

51
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.633
Aha! I knew it was you, Chespin! Sneaking around again!

52
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.933
So, that’s Chespin, huh?

53
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.633
Yes. It’s one of three Pokémon new Trainers can choose from!

54
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.700
The three Pokémon are Froakie, who’s a Water type,

55
00:03:13.766 --> 00:03:17.866
Fennekin, a Fire type, and the third one is Chespin, who’s a Grass type.

56
00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:20.766
Awesome. Chespin’s a Grass type!

57
00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.133
Chespin, the Spiny Nut Pokémon.

58
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.866
Chespin can flex the soft spikes on its head,

59
00:03:25.933 --> 00:03:29.133
making them so stiff and sharp they can even pierce through stone.

60
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.733
- Pika! Pikachu!
- Ches!

61
00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:33.166
It’s so cute!

62
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:36.466
If you wanted macaroons, you should have just said so!

63
00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:39.566
Why don’t you share?

64
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:42.566
Ches! Ches! Ches!

65
00:03:42.633 --> 00:03:45.666
- Huh?
- Pika?

66
00:03:45.733 --> 00:03:48.766
- I’m so sorry!
- Don’t worry!

67
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:51.133
That Chespin is a bit of a prankster.

68
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.533
I've got an idea! Let’s see what the professor’s doing, Bonnie.

69
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.066
Yeah! Let’s go!

70
00:04:04.733 --> 00:04:06.366
Target confirmed.

71
00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:09.366
How’s everyone feeling today?

72
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:12.200
All right, are you ready to go through with this, Meowth?

73
00:04:12.266 --> 00:04:15.066
- I’m ready to rock!
- Then let’s.

74
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:22.300
-Huh?

75
00:04:22.366 --> 00:04:26.366
- Well, if it isn’t the good professor.
- What are you doing here?

76
00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:30.400
See, Team Rocket needs to borrow you for a little bit, if you don’t mind.

77
00:04:30.466 --> 00:04:32.466
You! You’re that talking Meowth!

78
00:04:32.533 --> 00:04:34.233
And you’re toast!

79
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.800
What’s this all about?!

80
00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:41.133
You keep your evil hands off the Pokémon!

81
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.599
Huh! You’re the one we want. And you’re the one we’ve got!

82
00:04:45.666 --> 00:04:48.500
-In you go!

83
00:04:48.566 --> 00:04:51.599
- The catch of the day!
- Let’s scram out of here!

84
00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:54.966
- Huh? Isn’t that...
- Team Rocket! Let’s go after them!

85
00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:58.400
- Hm!
- Wait for me!

86
00:04:58.466 --> 00:05:00.099
Chespin? Chespin! Ches!

87
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.633
Na, Na!

88
00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.099
Hm!

89
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.599
- Professor!
- Hm?

90
00:05:08.666 --> 00:05:11.333
You’ve got to get out of here! Go back!

91
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.033
We’ll save you!

92
00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:18.833
Huh? Hey! Open the door! Open the door!

93
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.066
Ches? Chespin!

94
00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:29.233
Ches! Ches! Chespin! Chespin!

95
00:05:32.266 --> 00:05:35.633
- Serena, what do we do now?
- Huh?

96
00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.033
Ches!

97
00:05:38.099 --> 00:05:39.633
- Chespin!
- Pika, Pika!

98
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.666
- Chespin!
- Pika?

99
00:05:41.733 --> 00:05:43.133
Where is everyone?

100
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.900
- Ah! Professor Sycamore is missing!
- Serena and Bonnie, too!

101
00:05:46.966 --> 00:05:48.033
Chespin!

102
00:05:48.099 --> 00:05:50.300
Thanks, Chespin! We’ll take it from here!

103
00:05:50.366 --> 00:05:52.200
- Oh, no, poor Bonnie!
- I know what to do!

104
00:05:52.266 --> 00:05:55.033
Fletchling, I choose you!

105
00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:56.900
Fletchling, Fletchling, Fletchling!

106
00:05:56.966 --> 00:05:59.666
I’ll let Officer Jenny know what’s going on!

107
00:05:59.733 --> 00:06:02.400
- Thank you!
- Fletchling, follow that truck!

108
00:06:02.466 --> 00:06:04.233
Fletch! Fletchling!

109
00:06:11.366 --> 00:06:13.366
- Ches?
- What is it, Chespin?

110
00:06:13.433 --> 00:06:16.333
- Chespin!
- Huh?

111
00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.066
- Ches! Chespin!
- They’re pieces of macaroons.

112
00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:21.766
But why are they out here?

113
00:06:21.833 --> 00:06:24.933
Serena wanted us to find them, so she must have left a trail!

114
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.866
Yeah, you’re right and if we follow the macaroon trail,

115
00:06:27.933 --> 00:06:29.566
we’ll know where they were taken!

116
00:06:29.633 --> 00:06:30.733
Pika!

117
00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:36.733
- Ches! Ches!
- You’re doing great, Chespin!

118
00:06:38.966 --> 00:06:40.733
Phase one, complete.

119
00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:43.333
- No muss, no fuss!
- Right!

120
00:06:44.799 --> 00:06:47.533
- How did they get in?
- This isn’t your truck!

121
00:06:47.599 --> 00:06:52.533
Prepare for trouble! I’d say you bad people have finally met your match!

122
00:06:52.599 --> 00:06:55.033
And, make it a double crook catch!

123
00:06:55.099 --> 00:06:57.000
- To protect the world--
- Twerp thieves!

124
00:06:57.066 --> 00:06:59.066
Copyright infringement! Get away from him!

125
00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:02.266
You let us go now, or you’re going to wish you had!

126
00:07:02.333 --> 00:07:05.599
What a pain! You must be a Twerpette! Out!

127
00:07:05.666 --> 00:07:07.833
Or you’ll wish you had...

128
00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.433
Hey! You be quiet!

129
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:17.166
You’re in trouble! Dedenne, use Thunder Shock now!

130
00:07:17.233 --> 00:07:19.833
- Huh?
- Na, Na, Na!

131
00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:20.933
Ah!

132
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.366
Look, pal, all we want is your Mega Evolution secret.

133
00:07:24.433 --> 00:07:27.733
Spill the beans and we’ll let the bunch of you out of here!

134
00:07:27.799 --> 00:07:31.933
But if you want to be a dope and say no!

135
00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.200
So start quacking!

136
00:07:39.599 --> 00:07:44.766
Stop! All right! You win!

137
00:07:46.099 --> 00:07:49.233
The Mega Evolution data is in my coat pocket.

138
00:07:49.299 --> 00:07:50.966
In here?

139
00:07:51.966 --> 00:07:54.799
Look what I found! A memory card.

140
00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.299
-Clemont? Something wrong?

141
00:08:00.366 --> 00:08:03.866
Something terrible has happened! Oh!

142
00:08:03.933 --> 00:08:07.833
Ches! Chespin!

143
00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.066
Huh?

144
00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:11.799
- Pin!
- Fletchling!

145
00:08:11.866 --> 00:08:14.466
- Huh? It’s Fletchling!
- Fletchling!

146
00:08:24.933 --> 00:08:27.200
- There they are!
- Pika.

147
00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:31.200
So Team Rocket was behind this after all.

148
00:08:31.266 --> 00:08:33.266
What are you doing?

149
00:08:33.333 --> 00:08:37.199
Stifle your obnoxious Twerpish whining until our mission is complete.

150
00:08:37.266 --> 00:08:39.199
Ches!

151
00:08:41.666 --> 00:08:43.799
Pin? Ches, Ches, Ches! Pin?

152
00:08:43.866 --> 00:08:46.566
Hey, what do you think they’re doing?

153
00:08:46.633 --> 00:08:50.300
They’re probably trying to use my Mega Evolution data for no good.

154
00:08:50.366 --> 00:08:53.300
Huh? Then why did you give them that memory card?

155
00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:56.233
Well, I would have preferred not to,

156
00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.366
but keeping you safe is much more important to me.

157
00:09:00.433 --> 00:09:04.033
Eh? Ches, Ches!

158
00:09:05.233 --> 00:09:07.966
Eh! Ches!

159
00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:10.533
And in.

160
00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.466
So, after all that, do you think this will work?

161
00:09:13.533 --> 00:09:16.699
Of course. We simply input the Mega Evolution data

162
00:09:16.766 --> 00:09:20.966
into our secret weapon program and we’ll be good to go.

163
00:09:21.033 --> 00:09:23.733
Downloading.

164
00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:26.933
Hey, this gig is pumping me up big time!

165
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.366
- We’ve got to get them all out of there!
- Pika!

166
00:09:29.433 --> 00:09:33.033
Now, hold on. We can’t rush them, or we’ll get caught too!

167
00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:40.233
Ches! Pin, Pin, Pin, Pin, Pin!

168
00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.133
- Oh!
- Ches!

169
00:09:42.199 --> 00:09:46.066
- Chespin!
- Huh?

170
00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:49.433
It’s Chespin!!

171
00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.800
That did it!

172
00:09:50.866 --> 00:09:54.433
Heh, now that I think of it, rushing them is a great idea! Come on!

173
00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:58.500
- We’re going to get you out of here!
- Come on! Let’s go!

174
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.533
Who’s that Pokémon?

175
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.866
It’s Chespin!

176
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:18.833
Well, well! Why go chasing after Pikachu when Pikachu’s chasing us!

177
00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:21.633
Let our friends go free, Team Rocket!

178
00:10:21.699 --> 00:10:23.666
Prepare for trouble, you’re half right!

179
00:10:23.733 --> 00:10:26.333
That is our name, but your friends are stuck tight.

180
00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.433
To protect the world from devastation!

181
00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.233
To unite all people within our nation!

182
00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.500
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

183
00:10:34.566 --> 00:10:37.766
To extend our reach to the stars above!

184
00:10:37.833 --> 00:10:40.300
- Jessie!
- And James!

185
00:10:40.366 --> 00:10:42.833
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

186
00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:46.066
Surrender now or prepare for one Mega Evolved fight!

187
00:10:46.133 --> 00:10:49.500
- Meowth, that’s right!
- Wobbuff!

188
00:10:51.366 --> 00:10:52.733
That’s how it’s done.

189
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.166
- Serena, you okay?
- I’m fine!

190
00:10:55.233 --> 00:10:59.166
- Bonnie, did Team Rocket hurt you?
- I’m fine. Don’t worry.

191
00:10:59.233 --> 00:11:00.733
Could you untie me, too?

192
00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:05.333
We give you our totally awesome motto and you Twerps give us the brushoff!

193
00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.733
-Wobbuffet!

194
00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.266
Okay, let’s all get out of here!

195
00:11:10.333 --> 00:11:12.900
- That’s not going to happen.
- Huh?

196
00:11:14.066 --> 00:11:16.600
The mega software’s ready to roll, folks!

197
00:11:16.666 --> 00:11:21.366
Excellent! Now we can catch Pikachu the modern, Mega Evolution way!

198
00:11:21.433 --> 00:11:25.233
- Ready, Meowth?
- Thought you’d never ask!

199
00:11:28.366 --> 00:11:31.733
- What’s that?
- Oh, you’ll see soon enough.

200
00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:36.033
With the Mega Evolution data inputted into our secret weapon program,

201
00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.400
it’s now Mega Evolution times two!

202
00:11:38.466 --> 00:11:43.466
Or our magnificent Mega-Mega Meowth Machine!

203
00:11:43.533 --> 00:11:45.533
Activating program!

204
00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.900
What kind of machine is it?

205
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.433
Meowth, Meowth, Meowth!

206
00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.233
Rock and roll!

207
00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:58.000
Meowth!

208
00:11:59.466 --> 00:12:02.900
Oh, my! Marvelous! It looks powerful!

209
00:12:02.966 --> 00:12:06.966
Wow! I know they’re our enemy, but that's a super-cool invention!

210
00:12:07.033 --> 00:12:11.300
Stop! This isn’t exactly the time for the two of you to be impressed!

211
00:12:11.366 --> 00:12:13.199
- Right!
- Let’s get out of here!

212
00:12:13.266 --> 00:12:14.400
Come in, guys!

213
00:12:14.466 --> 00:12:16.466
-Pika!

214
00:12:16.533 --> 00:12:18.833
-Ches!

215
00:12:20.766 --> 00:12:24.000
Ches! Ches!

216
00:12:25.033 --> 00:12:27.466
Chespin, no! Huh?

217
00:12:27.533 --> 00:12:30.966
Ches!

218
00:12:31.033 --> 00:12:32.699
Ah!

219
00:12:40.866 --> 00:12:44.233
- Chespin, are you okay?
- Pin!

220
00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:47.733
I guess you must really like macaroons a lot!

221
00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.599
- Eh?
- Yeah, I’m okay. Thanks!

222
00:12:51.666 --> 00:12:54.500
Chespin? - Thank you.

223
00:12:54.566 --> 00:12:58.133
I feel much better!

224
00:12:58.199 --> 00:12:59.933
Chespin!

225
00:13:00.066 --> 00:13:03.166
We’ve got to figure out a way to stop that machine!

226
00:13:03.233 --> 00:13:05.000
My good friends are precious to me,

227
00:13:05.066 --> 00:13:10.000
just like those macaroons are precious to you! I’ve got to help them!

228
00:13:10.066 --> 00:13:13.599
Operation Pikachu Catch! Making it real!

229
00:13:15.199 --> 00:13:18.233
All right, Pikachu, use Thunderbolt!

230
00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:24.333
Pikachu!

231
00:13:26.733 --> 00:13:30.699
-Pika!

232
00:13:30.766 --> 00:13:32.199
Pikachu!

233
00:13:32.266 --> 00:13:36.766
This machine can reflect your Thunderbolt, which gives us the mega-upper hand.

234
00:13:36.833 --> 00:13:40.166
No way! There’s got to be something we can do.

235
00:13:40.233 --> 00:13:41.900
Pin?

236
00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.199
- Chespin! Pin!
- Huh?

237
00:13:47.733 --> 00:13:49.199
Pin, Pin!

238
00:13:51.199 --> 00:13:54.333
What’s that?

239
00:13:56.166 --> 00:13:58.699
-Pikachu!

240
00:13:58.766 --> 00:14:02.066
Now, let’s make not catching Pikachu a thing of the past!

241
00:14:02.133 --> 00:14:05.766
- Talk about a mega-mega blast!
- This one’s for the Boss!

242
00:14:05.833 --> 00:14:10.666
We’ll hand him the most powerful Pikachu he’s ever seen!

243
00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:18.400
This thing is plugged in!

244
00:14:18.466 --> 00:14:20.699
- Ches! Pin!
- I see!

245
00:14:20.766 --> 00:14:21.900
Pin!

246
00:14:21.966 --> 00:14:24.766
Pikachu!

247
00:14:24.833 --> 00:14:27.266
- Argh!
- Pika!

248
00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:30.033
- No, Ash!
- Get out of there, Ash!

249
00:14:33.733 --> 00:14:35.533
- Huh?
- Pika?

250
00:14:35.599 --> 00:14:39.033
Now, what’s wrong? Where’s the juice?

251
00:14:39.099 --> 00:14:42.033
- Some sort of blackout?
- Sure seems that way!

252
00:14:42.099 --> 00:14:44.033
- Huh?
- Pika?

253
00:14:44.099 --> 00:14:47.766
Ches!

254
00:14:47.833 --> 00:14:53.533
- What do I do to fix this thing?!
- Turn on the auxiliary power!

255
00:14:53.599 --> 00:14:56.466
10-4! Extra juice, you’re up!

256
00:14:58.466 --> 00:15:01.533
Connecting power to main engine, now!

257
00:15:06.666 --> 00:15:08.099
Meowth!

258
00:15:08.166 --> 00:15:11.300
I’ll say one thing. They’re prepared!

259
00:15:11.366 --> 00:15:14.599
- Chespin!
- Huh? Hm.

260
00:15:14.666 --> 00:15:17.500
- Chespin! Use Pin Missile!
- Ches!

261
00:15:19.166 --> 00:15:23.433
Chespin!

262
00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.633
Pin, Pin, Pin, Pin!

263
00:15:26.699 --> 00:15:28.933
No use. It’s not working.

264
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:32.666
- Chespin! Pin!
- Hm.

265
00:15:32.733 --> 00:15:37.933
- Right! Use Tackle!
- Ches, Ches, Ches, Chespin!

266
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.433
It’s too strong. You can’t beat it!

267
00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.933
Thanks! That kind of tickled a little!

268
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:48.166
Chespin! Chespin!

269
00:15:48.233 --> 00:15:50.933
- Go for it, Chespin!
- Pika, Pika!

270
00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:54.333
- Look at it go!
- Pikachu! Pika! Pik!

271
00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:56.566
Good idea! You two together!

272
00:15:56.633 --> 00:15:59.199
Pikachu! Quick Attack!

273
00:15:59.266 --> 00:16:01.400
- Pika, Pika!
- Ches!

274
00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:09.000
- Ches, Ches, Ches, Ches Pin!
- Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik, Pik, Pika!

275
00:16:09.066 --> 00:16:11.033
Keep it up, Twerp Pokémon!

276
00:16:11.099 --> 00:16:13.633
But you’re no match for Mega-Mega Meowth!

277
00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:20.266
What was that?

278
00:16:23.199 --> 00:16:24.766
- Huh?
- Check it out!

279
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.666
- I remember them!
- Incredible!

280
00:16:30.966 --> 00:16:34.133
Uh-oh! Mega Blaziken!

281
00:16:36.033 --> 00:16:37.966
Use Flamethrower, now!

282
00:16:38.033 --> 00:16:41.533
Mega Blaze!

283
00:16:41.599 --> 00:16:44.066
It’s getting warm in here!

284
00:16:54.533 --> 00:16:57.466
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- It’s charbroiled!

285
00:16:57.533 --> 00:17:01.533
Both sides are Mega Evolved, but the machine got barbecued in one shot.

286
00:17:06.099 --> 00:17:08.099
Now, Pikachu, Electro Ball!

287
00:17:08.166 --> 00:17:11.099
I’m sure your Pin Missile will work now, Chespin!

288
00:17:11.166 --> 00:17:15.866
- Ches!
- Pika, Pika! Pikachu!

289
00:17:19.666 --> 00:17:23.366
-Sounds like it’s making tea.

290
00:17:23.433 --> 00:17:26.566
Mega-Mega Meowth’s power core took a direct hit!

291
00:17:26.633 --> 00:17:29.533
Is that the whistling sound of impending doom?

292
00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.133
If so, you know what’s next.

293
00:17:33.433 --> 00:17:38.833
- We’re blasting off again!
- Wobbuffet!

294
00:17:40.433 --> 00:17:41.933
And don’t come back!

295
00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:44.966
- We did it, Clemont!
- Yeah!

296
00:17:45.033 --> 00:17:48.000
-Mega Blaziken was awesome.

297
00:17:49.933 --> 00:17:53.366
Chespin and Pikachu were pretty awesome, too!

298
00:17:55.066 --> 00:17:57.533
- Ches.
- You know what?

299
00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:00.433
I think you deserve a little reward.

300
00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:03.433
- Yummy macaroons!
- Ches!

301
00:18:05.133 --> 00:18:07.666
Ches! Huh?

302
00:18:07.733 --> 00:18:10.166
Chespin, Pin, Pin, Ches!

303
00:18:11.866 --> 00:18:13.366
- Pin!
- Yay!

304
00:18:13.433 --> 00:18:15.733
- For me?
- Pika!

305
00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:16.633
Thank you!

306
00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:20.800
Thanks, Chespin! Be careful or there won’t be any left for you!

307
00:18:20.866 --> 00:18:22.300
Pin, Chespin, Pin, Pin!

308
00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.800
It’s good that Clemont and Bonnie are traveling with Ash and company.

309
00:18:28.866 --> 00:18:32.533
Strength isn’t the only thing Trainers needs for greatness.

310
00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:34.600
Great Trainers also need to forge

311
00:18:34.666 --> 00:18:37.800
an important and lasting bond with their Pokémon!

312
00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:45.700
Thank you so much for your help today. Because of all of you, I’m free again!

313
00:18:45.766 --> 00:18:49.300
Yeah, but still, your research lab’s messed up again.

314
00:18:50.899 --> 00:18:52.800
Pika! Pikachu!

315
00:18:52.866 --> 00:18:57.300
Not to worry. I’ll have it all fixed by the time you come to visit again.

316
00:18:57.366 --> 00:18:58.833
We will, no doubt!

317
00:18:58.899 --> 00:19:00.700
Guess we’d better get going.

318
00:19:00.766 --> 00:19:03.866
- Great to see you again!
- Big brother, excuse me!

319
00:19:03.933 --> 00:19:06.166
Hm? Bonnie, is there something wrong?

320
00:19:06.233 --> 00:19:09.766
Look over there. It’s been watching us.

321
00:19:09.833 --> 00:19:16.300
Chespin? You were a big help, Chespin. I’m sure that we’ll see you soon!

322
00:19:16.366 --> 00:19:20.866
- Ches! Chespin, Pin, Pin, Ches!
- Huh?

323
00:19:20.933 --> 00:19:23.366
Pin?

324
00:19:23.433 --> 00:19:28.133
You know, Clemont, it looks to me like Chespin wants to go with you.

325
00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:32.866
Hm, it’s an amazing thing to watch the likes of you and Ash when you’re together.

326
00:19:32.933 --> 00:19:34.866
Huh?

327
00:19:34.933 --> 00:19:36.866
- Clemont?
- Huh?

328
00:19:36.933 --> 00:19:41.633
I want to travel with Chespin, too! Please! Please! Please!

329
00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:45.566
Is that okay? Would you let me bring Chespin along with us?

330
00:19:45.633 --> 00:19:50.033
Of course! After all, that’s what Chespin wants.

331
00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:54.500
I happen to have Chespin’s Poké Ball right here with me. It’s yours!

332
00:19:54.566 --> 00:20:00.533
Hm! So, Professor Sycamore says it’s okay for you to come along with us.

333
00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.433
Chespin!

334
00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:07.033
That’s great! Now, it’s a pleasure to meet you all over again!

335
00:20:14.866 --> 00:20:20.233
Yes! Today is a great day, thanks to science! I caught Chespin!

336
00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:22.233
Chespin’s a keeper, too!

337
00:20:23.233 --> 00:20:26.733
- Now, off to Cyllage City!
- Pika!

338
00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.933
Take care, Professor Sycamore! Bye!

339
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.133
- Bye, bye!
- Huh? Time for adventure!

340
00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:34.566
Goodbye!

341
00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:37.766
Our heroes have a new friend in Chespin!

342
00:20:37.833 --> 00:20:39.566
Now, they’re off to Cyllage City,

343
00:20:39.633 --> 00:20:42.933
where Ash takes his next step towards entering the Kalos League,

344
00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.300
as the journey continues!
